course: dictionary
lesson: 12336
title: Courtyard: an open space inside walls
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A courtyard is an open space with no roof, surrounded by walls or buildings. It is outside in the sense that the sky is above it, but it is still inside a bigger place.
explain: «The knights gathered in the castle courtyard.» The words castle and walls tell you the courtyard is inside the castle, with the sky above and stone all around.
explain: «The carts rolled into the inn courtyard.» An inn is a place where travellers stay, so the courtyard is the open yard inside it. Many schools have a courtyard too, where children play at break time.
fact: A courtyard is an open space with no roof.
fact: A courtyard is surrounded by walls or buildings.
fact: Courtyards can be found inside castles, houses, schools, inns and palaces.
fact: Phrases you may see: in the courtyard, the castle courtyard.
fact: Courtyard is a noun, and its plural is courtyards.
exercise: «The knights lined up in the castle courtyard.» What is a courtyard? | *An open space with no roof, surrounded by walls | A river that runs past the castle | A tall tower with a flag on top | A dark room under the ground
exercise: «The rain fell on the school courtyard all afternoon.» Why was the courtyard wet? | Because it was under a heavy roof | *Because it has no roof, so the rain falls on it | Because the children had washed it | Because it was inside a cave
exercise: Which of these places can have a courtyard? | *A palace | A puddle | A pencil | A cloud
test: «The old palace had a beautiful courtyard with a fountain.» What is a courtyard? | A street of shops | *An open space with no roof, inside walls | A kind of small boat | A small room for coats and boots
test: Which place can have a courtyard inside it? | A raincloud | *A school | A bicycle bell | A teaspoon
exam: «Ella ran across the courtyard to meet her friend.» Which meaning fits courtyard best? | A narrow corridor with a low ceiling | A garden with a fence and a gate | *An open space with no roof, surrounded by walls or buildings | A room where food is cooked
